      [
        "Working Principle",
        "Skip is a hoisting container directly loaded with valuable ore, waste rock and gangue. It is divided into vertical‑shaft type and inclined‑shaft type. For main‑shaft skips, classified by hoist type: single‑rope skip and multi‑rope skip. Classified by unloading mode: bottom‑dump type and tipping‑dump type for vertical shafts; rear‑dump type and tipping‑dump type for inclined shafts. Bottom‑dump skips are adopted for coal mine vertical shafts, rear‑dump for inclined shafts. Tipping‑dump skips are used for drum‑winding hoisting in metal mines, while bottom‑dump skips for multi‑rope friction hoisting. Skips for balanced hoisting are equipped with tail‑rope suspension device; multi‑rope skips are fitted with steel‑rope tension balancing device.",
